00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.899
than using money to hire people using the
money to increase salaries using the tax cut

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:43.229
for all of the types of winning that we were
told would come from Donald Trump's tax guts.

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:48.600
Now Texas instruments did make a modest increase
to their capital expenses, some of which would

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:54.210
be reasonably said to fall under the umbrella
of reinvesting in the company, but it's small

00:01:54.210 --> 00:02:00.450
potatoes compared to the billions that went
into just buying back shares of stock and

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:05.390
it's one of those stories where yet none of
it is surprising like if you were paying attention,

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:09.330
this is exactly what we were predicting. This
is what always happens and it's going to get

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:14.940
even worse. Check out this chart comparing
hourly wages to productivity.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:19.810
What you might notice, and I'll describe it
to you, is that up until about 1973 wages

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:25.320
and productivity went up basically in parallel
as workers became more productive, their wages

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:31.630
went up roughly in proportion to those productivity
increases. And then in 1973 that splits and

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:38.390
hourly wages go up. Only 9% since 1973 while
productivity is up 72% now this is partially

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:44.930
technology and this is why the interests of
workers and their employers are no longer

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:50.990
aligned for lots of companies, their biggest
